1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,853
Every new Claude Code session starts

2
00:00:01,873 --> 00:00:04,300
with a fresh context, like day one on the job.

3
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:06,625
The course says that without CLAUDE.md, it re-explores

4
00:00:06,645 --> 00:00:09,490
your structure, dependencies and finished features.

5
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:11,814
The fix is a Markdown file in your project root,

6
00:00:11,834 --> 00:00:14,390
read automatically at the start of every session.

7
00:00:14,410 --> 00:00:17,590
Anthropic's analogy: an onboarding script for your codebase.

8
00:00:17,610 --> 00:00:19,908
What goes in? Commands

9
00:00:19,928 --> 00:00:22,060
and style rules it can't guess from the code,

10
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:23,950
and keep each file under 200 lines.

11
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:26,520
The project file goes into version control for the team;

12
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:29,430
the user file lives in your config folder, just for you.

13
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:32,900
They stack when read; one doesn't override another.

14
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,979
Correct the same mistake twice and it's time to write it down,

15
00:00:34,999 --> 00:00:36,730
like use server actions instead of API routes.

16
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:37,993
To get it into the file,

17
00:00:38,013 --> 00:00:39,603
say add this to CLAUDE.md.

18
00:00:39,623 --> 00:00:42,370
Just saying remember saves it to Claude's own memory.

19
00:00:42,390 --> 00:00:44,428
Reference project docs with @ and a path,

20
00:00:44,448 --> 00:00:46,834
though they still load in full at launch

21
00:00:46,854 --> 00:00:48,780
and don't save context.

22
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:51,539
The course also suggests starting without one,

23
00:00:51,559 --> 00:00:55,080
seeing where you keep correcting it, then running /init.

24
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:57,275
But it's context, not enforced configuration.

25
00:00:57,295 --> 00:01:00,100
Rules that must always hold belong in a hook.
